From a7c8b289fb6770ba5913fe2e0b3b2c9289a0e545 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pooya Parsa <pooya@pi0.io>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 10:16:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wasm: advertise the riscv ISA of kwemu and answer
 riscv_hwprobe

User space picks code paths from riscv_hwprobe and the "isa" line of
/proc/cpuinfo, so both come from one table in cpu.c, in the canonical
order of riscv_isa_ext[]: RV64GC, the extensions every kwemu has
(Zicbop, Ziccamoa, Ziccif, Zicclsm, Ziccrse, Zicntr, Zihintntl,
Zihintpause, Za64rs, Zaamo, Zalrsc, Zca, Zcd), and the optional ones the
kwemu build implements (KW_ISA_* bits: the scalar extensions of
RVA23U64 plus Zbc, Zbkb, Zbkc, Zbkx, Zknd and Zkne), each with its hwprobe
bit in IMA_EXT_0 or, for the platform properties, IMA_EXT_1. Zkt is not
listed: kwemu's AES instructions look the S-box up by data.
kw_isa_init() picks the set once at boot, right after kw_cpu_init().

kw.isa= is a comma list applied from left to right: "rv64gc" turns off
everything beyond RV64GC, "-ext" turns one extension off, "+ext" turns
it back on if kwemu implements it (kw.isa=rv64gc, kw.isa=-zbc,-zkne,
kw.isa=rv64gc,+zbb). It is meant for A/B measurements and bisecting.

riscv_hwprobe answers as riscv does: the CBO block sizes are 64 while
the extension is listed, MISALIGNED_SCALAR_PERF is FAST (one unaligned
host access), MISALIGNED_VECTOR_PERF is UNSUPPORTED (no V),
HIGHEST_VIRT_ADDRESS is STACK_TOP_MAX (Sv39), the vendor extension keys
are 0, and TIME_CSR_FREQ stays unknown because the time CSR counts
instructions. RISCV_HWPROBE_WHICH_CPUS is answered as a plain query.
AT_HWCAP stays IMAFDC. riscv_flush_icache drops kwemu's translations.

The uapi <asm/hwprobe.h> is arch/riscv's from Linux 7.3.

Signed-off-by: Pooya Parsa <pooya@pi0.io>
---
 arch/wasm/include/asm/hwcap.h        |  28 ++++
 arch/wasm/include/uapi/asm/hwprobe.h | 131 ++++++++++++++++
 arch/wasm/kernel/cpu.c               | 221 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 arch/wasm/kernel/sys_riscv.c         | 115 ++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 495 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 arch/wasm/include/asm/hwcap.h
 create mode 100644 arch/wasm/include/uapi/asm/hwprobe.h
 create mode 100644 arch/wasm/kernel/cpu.c
 create mode 100644 arch/wasm/kernel/sys_riscv.c

